  "description": {
    "ja": {
      "source": "Wikipedia 日本語版「リベリカコーヒーノキ」",
      "source_url": "https://ja.wikipedia.org/wiki/%E3%83%AA%E3%83%99%E3%83%AA%E3%82%AB%E3%82%B3%E3%83%BC%E3%83%92%E3%83%BC%E3%83%8E%E3%82%AD",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-09",
      "revision": 109917898,
      "text": "リベリカコーヒーノキ は、西アフリカのリベリア原産のリンドウ目アカネ科の植物である。アラビカコーヒーノキやロブスタコーヒーノキとともにコーヒー3原種に数えられるが、消費量は少なく世界全体の流通量の1パーセントに満たない。"
    },
    "en": {
      "source": "Wikipedia 英語版「Coffea liberica」",
      "source_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Coffea_liberica",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-09",
      "revision": 1378276004,
      "text": "Coffea liberica, commonly known as Liberian coffee, is a species of flowering plant in the family Rubiaceae from which coffee is produced. It is native to western and central Africa, and has become naturalised in areas including Colombia, Venezuela, the Philippines, Sumatra, Borneo and Java."
    }
